*** Add File: README.md
+# Figma Link MCP
+
+This workspace contains a minimal MCP server for parsing Figma links.
+
+## What it does
+
+- `parse_figma_link`: extracts the Figma link type, file key, title slug, node id, query params, and the likely Figma API targets.
+- `get_figma_data`: if `FIGMA_TOKEN` is available, fetches either the linked node summary or the file page list from the Figma REST API.
+
+## Why this approach
+
+The current environment does not expose a built-in Figma MCP server, so this project provides a lightweight local fallback focused on the main need: understanding and resolving Figma prototype URLs.
+
+## Run it
+
+```powershell
+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\figma-mcp.ps1
+```
+
+The server speaks JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout and implements the MCP methods:
+
+- `initialize`
+- `tools/list`
+- `tools/call`
+
+## Example tool call
+
+```json
+{
+  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
+  "id": 2,
+  "method": "tools/call",
+  "params": {
+    "name": "parse_figma_link",
+    "arguments": {
+      "url": "https://www.figma.com/design/NdIFQRMnOPTlx59LrH0SXu/Untitled?t=30DHp9jQL9pBntcv-0"
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Optional Figma API access
+
+Set `FIGMA_TOKEN` before starting the server:
+
+```powershell
+$env:FIGMA_TOKEN = "your-figma-personal-access-token"
+```
+
+Then call `get_figma_data` with the same URL.
*** End Patch

